This is the single append-only execution-status record for all plan phases
and steps. Initialization does not claim that P0.1 or any phase has started
or completed. Previously accepted work is recorded only after its evidence
is reconciled with the canonical plan.

RECORDING RULES
- Append a PHASE START entry with the phase number and title at phase start.
- Begin every step entry with its phase and exact step ID, e.g. Phase 0 / P0.1.
- Append separate START, VALIDATION, BLOCKED, FAILURE, ACCEPTANCE, or ADDENDUM
  events as appropriate; never replace an earlier entry.
- Use UTC timestamps and READY, GATED, BLOCKED, DEFERRED, IN PROGRESS, or DONE.
- Record all prerequisites and the baseline before implementation begins.
- Use pending for unverified information; never infer success or acceptance.
- Mark DONE only after persistent evidence and user acceptance are recorded.
- Append PHASE GATE ACCEPTANCE with every required step and criterion accounted
  for before beginning the next phase.
- Link durable raw logs, CI artifacts, commits, and freezes from this record.
- Exclude secrets, credentials, key contributions, and protected metadata.

