Implemented behavior / required six-surface audit:
  1. SnpKeyContributionV1:
     Exists in the untracked codec; 220-byte context plus envelope and 32-byte
     secret totals 272 bytes; strict decoding and zeroizing ownership exist.
     Still uses old tenant_report_id/contribution_commitment/local_policy_digest
     semantics. It is not a commitment-preimage verifier or authenticated
     runtime exchange. Reconcile under P0.3/P0.7; activate under Task 10.
  2. Opcodes 0x26 and 0x27:
     Exist as ExchangeSnpKeyContributionReq/Rsp. Static layout tests pass.
     Responder runtime match still rejects unhandled SNP opcodes with an
     explicit error. Allocations do not claim runtime activation.
  3. Element type 0x0104:
     Exists as SnpKeyContributionV1; one 272-byte element, 282-byte framed
     message, unchanged application-size cap. Preserve exact allocation.
  4. SnpAuthorizationResultV1:
     Committed 88-byte strict destination decision/failure/digest codec exists;
     no delta to its source file in this baseline. It is not key confirmation
     or installation acknowledgement. Runtime appraisal/history binding stays
     gated on P0.6/P0.8 and Tasks 8-9.
  5. Complete 64-byte REPORT_DATA:
     Validator checks digest plus all 16 padding bytes. Captured-fixture path
     derives its expected digest from the fixture itself, not the live TH1.
     ReportDataContextV1 still admits only purposes 0x01-0x03, Source/
     Destination roles, and AES algorithm; local handoff/recovery registries,
     new field semantics, and purpose-specific digest checks are not complete.
     Current P0.3 contract is frozen; implementation reconciliation remains.
  6. MigrationKeyInstaller:
     Existing trait accepts SnpOperationContext plus a key slice and returns
     Result<(), PalError>; session calls the mock installer with 32 key bytes.
     Does not yet carry exact VeniceV1 history, algorithm, authenticated tenant
     identity, typed install outcome, or durable firmware-backed persistence.
     Complete interface under T4.11, emulator semantics under Tasks 11-12,
     and hardware behavior under H5.3.

