User design disposition (verbatim):
  "Implement proposed record/state conformance; retain crypto, persistence and SPDM scheduling gates"
User conditions (verbatim): "None".
Approved design:
  Confirmation record type 0x0006, element 0x0105, 128 bytes, shared by
  destination/source tags. Installation record type 0x0007, element 0x0106,
  136 bytes. Bind request, role/direction, canonical session-context digest
  and typed status. Confirmation includes 48-byte tag, zero for rejection.
  Result distinguishes Succeeded/Failed/Aborted/Indeterminate and encodes
  optional actual raw firmware status without treating absent as success.
  Success reuses the P0.3 installation-result digest; non-success digest zero.
  Destination confirmation precedes source confirmation; success result
  additionally requires verified fresh persisted-state evidence.
  Negative outcomes can terminate earlier without waiting for success evidence.
  Unavailable confirmation/persistence verification fails closed.
Mandatory deferred gates:
  Authoritative Task 2 session/HMAC/KDF construction and independent crypto
  vectors at P0.10/Task 10; qualified persisted-state verifier at Task 12;
  actual SPDM request/response scheduling and opcode allocations at
  P0.11/T4.12. Elements are reserved, but no new opcode or runtime dispatch
  is activated. Record/state oracles are not cryptographic or firmware proof.
Status: IN PROGRESS; no commit, push or runtime activation.

